    </item>
    <item>
      <title>TNS to Tackle Cross-Channel Fraud and Customer Trust in Two Sessions at CFCA Fall Educational 2026</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:18:00 UT</pubDate>
      <enclosure url="https://mms.businesswire.com/media/20260925393273/en/1271591/21/CORP_PNG_TNS_Logo_GBL_NOV2021.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="2048"/>
      <description>RESTON, Va.--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- #CFCAFall2026--Communications fraud rarely stays in one lane. Bad actors move across voice, messaging, email, applications and social media – spoofing financial institutions’ phone numbers to impersonate them and defraud customers, and exploiting the fact that the intelligence needed to stop them is often scattered across platforms, companies, industries, countries and continents. The result is a widening trust gap where consumers have grown wary of even legitimate outreach from</description>
      <link>http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260925393273/en/TNS-to-Tackle-Cross-Channel-Fraud-and-Customer-Trust-in-Two-Sessions-at-CFCA-Fall-Educational-2026/?feedref=JjAwJuNHiystnCoBq_hl-V2wqxRmnpgZtOypyHtjMYiqcp-o_pnudlUwsb5apQ1S4gUE65BTfjH3-pSuqdv0gW3cb3F4oTIgUqCPafFkgu4s9L7CzgBlYMXxVoyWhzlQ</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">20260925393273en</guid>
    </item>
    <item>
